{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HFBmeQp5b7LqSaDte8QPKc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd015-basename\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/basename: Strip Directory and Suffix from Filenames\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts extract filename components from paths using basename. The macOS BSD\n6\t  basename differs from GNU basename in multi-argument support (-a flag) and NUL-delimited\n7\t  output (-z flag). The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n8\t  (gbasename, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge\n9\t  cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Strip the directory component from one or more file paths, outputting only the final path component.\n13\t  - G2: Support optional suffix removal from the result.\n14\t  - G3: Support multi-argument mode (-a) for processing multiple paths in a single invocation.\n15\t  - G4: Support NUL-delimited output (-z) for safe handling of filenames containing newlines.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Single-argument mode (default)\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: \"When invoked as 'basename NAME', must strip the longest prefix ending in '/' from NAME and print the result followed by a newline.\"\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: \"When invoked as 'basename NAME SUFFIX', must strip the directory prefix and then remove SUFFIX from the end of the result if it matches. SUFFIX is a literal string match, not a pattern.\"\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: Must strip trailing slashes from NAME before processing. Multiple consecutive trailing slashes are all removed.\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: \"When NAME consists entirely of slashes, must output '/'.\"\n29\t      - R1.5:\n30\t          text: When NAME is an empty string, must output an empty line (newline only).\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Multi-argument mode (-a, --multiple)\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: -a or --multiple must enable processing of multiple NAME arguments. Each NAME is processed independently and the result is printed on a separate line.\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: -s SUFFIX or --suffix=SUFFIX must remove SUFFIX from each result and implies -a. When -s is given, the second positional argument is treated as a NAME, not a SUFFIX.\n39\t      - R2.3:\n40\t          text: In multi-argument mode without -s, no suffix removal is performed on any argument.\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: Each result must be followed by a newline character, or by a NUL byte (0x00) if -z or --zero is given.\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: Must exit 1 when called with an incorrect number of arguments in single-argument mode (zero arguments or more than two without -a).\n51\t      - R3.4:\n52\t          text: Must print an error message to stderr when argument validation fails.\n53\t\n54\t  R4:\n55\t    title: Differential testing\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R4.1:\n58\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n59\t      - R4.2:\n60\t          text: \"Tests must cover: simple path (dir/file), trailing slashes, root path (/), empty string, suffix removal, multi-argument mode (-a), suffix mode (-s), and NUL-delimited output (-z).\"\n61\t      - R4.3:\n62\t          text: Tests must verify error output and exit code for invalid argument counts.\n63\t\n64\tnon_goals:\n65\t  - cmd/basename does not implement pattern-based suffix removal (glob or regex); suffix is a literal string match.\n66\t  - cmd/basename does not read from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n67\t  - cmd/basename does not handle encoding; paths are treated as byte sequences with '/' as the separator.\n68\t\n69\tacceptance_criteria:\n70\t  - id: AC1\n71\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename /usr/bin/sort produces 'sort', matching gbasename.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R1.4\n77\t      - R1.5\n78\t  - id: AC2\n79\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename include/stdio.h .h produces 'stdio', matching gbasename.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R1.1\n82\t      - R1.2\n83\t      - R1.3\n84\t      - R1.4\n85\t      - R1.5\n86\t  - id: AC3\n87\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename -a /usr/bin/sort /usr/bin/cat produces 'sort' and 'cat' on separate lines, matching gbasename -a.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R2.1\n90\t      - R2.2\n91\t      - R3.3\n92\t      - R4.2\n93\t  - id: AC4\n94\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename -s .h include/stdio.h include/stdlib.h produces 'stdio' and 'stdlib' on separate lines.\"\n95\t    traces:\n96\t      - R2.2\n97\t      - R2.3\n98\t      - R4.2\n99\t  - id: AC5\n100\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gbasename passes for simple paths, trailing slashes, root, empty string, suffix removal, -a, -s, and -z modes.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.5\n103\t      - R2.1\n104\t      - R2.2\n105\t      - R2.3\n106\t      - R3.1\n107\t      - R3.3\n108\t      - R4.1\n109\t      - R4.2\n110\t  - id: AC6\n111\t    criterion: \"cmd/basename compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n112\t    traces:\n113\t      - R1.1\n114\t      - R1.2\n115\t      - R1.3\n116\t      - R1.4\n117\t      - R1.5\n118\t      - R2.1\n119\t      - R2.2\n120\t      - R2.3\n121\t      - R3.1\n122\t      - R3.2\n123\t      - R3.3\n124\t      - R3.4\n125\t      - R4.1\n126\t      - R4.2\n127\t      - R4.3\n128\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abe39796-3a16-4ddb-b1e5-30fe142bd70a","uuid":"c62fb772-8fd8-4eb3-98b3-897901833735","timestamp":"2026-05-14T03:35:14.579Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5138/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd015-basename.yaml","content":"id: srd015-basename\ntitle: \"cmd/basename: Strip Directory and Suffix from Filenames\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts extract filename components from paths using basename. The macOS BSD\n  basename differs from GNU basename in multi-argument support (-a flag) and NUL-delimited\n  output (-z flag). The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gbasename, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations and edge\n  cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Strip the directory component from one or more file paths, outputting only the final path component.\n  - G2: Support optional suffix removal from the result.\n  - G3: Support multi-argument mode (-a) for processing multiple paths in a single invocation.\n  - G4: Support NUL-delimited output (-z) for safe handling of filenames containing newlines.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Single-argument mode (default)\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"When invoked as 'basename NAME', must strip the longest prefix ending in '/' from NAME and print the result followed by a newline.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"When invoked as 'basename NAME SUFFIX', must strip the directory prefix and then remove SUFFIX from the end of the result if it matches. SUFFIX is a literal string match, not a pattern.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must strip trailing slashes from NAME before processing. Multiple consecutive trailing slashes are all removed.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"When NAME consists entirely of slashes, must output '/'.\"\n      - R1.5:\n          text: When NAME is an empty string, must output an empty line (newline only).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Multi-argument mode (-a, --multiple)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -a or --multiple must enable processing of multiple NAME arguments. Each NAME is processed independently and the result is printed on a separate line.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: -s SUFFIX or --suffix=SUFFIX must remove SUFFIX from each result and implies -a. When -s is given, the second positional argument is treated as a NAME, not a SUFFIX.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: In multi-argument mode without -s, no suffix removal is performed on any argument.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Each result must be followed by a newline character, or by a NUL byte (0x00) if -z or --zero is given.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 when called with an incorrect number of arguments in single-argument mode (zero arguments or more than two without -a).\n      - R3.4:\n          text: Must print an error message to stderr when argument validation fails.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: simple path (dir/file), trailing slashes, root path (/), empty string, suffix removal, multi-argument mode (-a), suffix mode (-s), and NUL-delimited output (-z).\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify error output and exit code for invalid argument counts.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/basename does not implement pattern-based suffix removal (glob or regex); suffix is a literal string match.\n  - cmd/basename does not read from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n  - cmd/basename does not handle encoding; paths are treated as byte sequences with '/' as the separator.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename /usr/bin/sort produces 'sort', matching gbasename.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename include/stdio.h .h produces 'stdio', matching gbasename.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename -a /usr/bin/sort /usr/bin/cat produces 'sort' and 'cat' on separate lines, matching gbasename -a.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/basename -s .h include/stdio.h include/stdlib.h produces 'stdio' and 'stdlib' on separate lines.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gbasename passes for simple paths, trailing slashes, root, empty string, suffix removal, -a, -s, and -z modes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.5\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/basename compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":128,"startLine":1,"totalLines":128}}}
